---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import HeroDiaporama from '../../components/HeroDiaporama.astro';
import Galerie from '../../components/Galerie.astro';
import Faq from '../../components/Faq.astro';
import Invitation from '../../components/Invitation.astro';
import { img, bandeau, HERO_MARIAGE } from '../../lib/photos';

const photosHero = bandeau(HERO_MARIAGE);

// Même sélection et même ordre que la page française : chaque lieu du fonds une fois.
const photos = [
  ['maries-jeu-d-ombre-couloir-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'The couple caught in a play of light and shadow at the end of a corridor'],
  ['mariee-allee-de-palmiers-bassin-marrakech-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'The bride in the avenue of palms beside the pool, Marrakech'],
  ['fou-rire-noir-et-blanc-jardins-coppelia-honfleur-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'The couple in fits of laughter, black and white, Coppélia gardens near Honfleur'],
  ['maries-etreinte-crepuscule-plage-santa-giulia-corse-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'The couple embracing at dusk, Santa Giulia beach, Corsica'],
  ['preparatifs-chaussures-dior-chateau-champlatreux-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'The bride’s shoes during the preparations, château de Champlâtreux'],
  ['escalier-colimacon-noir-et-blanc-trouville-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'The couple in the spiral staircase, black and white, Trouville'],
  ['mariee-sourire-voile-jardin-grand-courtoiseau-loiret-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'The bride smiling beneath her veil, gardens of the Grand Courtoiseau, Loiret'],
  ['maries-plage-ciel-crepuscule-ile-maurice-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'The couple on the beach under a dusk sky, Mauritius'],
  ['voile-parc-chateau-pont-chevron-noir-et-blanc-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'Veil unfurled in the park of a Loire Valley château, black and white'],
  ['diner-guirlandes-lumineuses-patio-andalousie-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'Dinner under festoon lights in the patio, Andalusia'],
  ['grand-escalier-entree-maries-chateau-saint-martin-du-tertre-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'The couple entering down the grand staircase of a French château'],
  ['baiser-sous-le-voile-vitrail-bruxelles-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'A kiss under the veil in front of a stained-glass window, Brussels'],
  ['mariee-arche-fleurie-plage-seychelles-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'The bride beneath the flower arch on the beach, Seychelles'],
  ['houppa-crepuscule-chateau-la-bourdaisiere-montlouis-sur-loire-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'Ceremony beneath the chuppah at dusk, château de la Bourdaisière, Loire Valley'],
  ['mariee-voile-lumiere-chaude-chateau-de-vallery-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'The bride beneath her veil in warm light, château de Vallery'],
  ['maries-pont-bir-hakeim-tour-eiffel-paris-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'The couple on the pont de Bir-Hakeim facing the Eiffel Tower, black and white'],
  ['ceremonie-houppa-parc-chateau-baronville-beville-le-comte-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'Ceremony beneath the chuppah in the park of the château de Baronville'],
  ['seance-jour-d-apres-vagues-deauville-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'Day-after session in the waves at Deauville, black and white'],
  ['maries-rochers-ciel-orageux-domaine-murtoli-corse-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'The couple on the rocks under a storm sky, Domaine de Murtoli, Corsica'],
  ['mariee-colonnade-lanternes-palais-royal-paris-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'Bride alone beneath the colonnade and lanterns of the Palais-Royal in Paris'],
  ['bain-nocturne-piscine-palmiers-marrakech-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'Night swim in the lit pool among the palms, Marrakech'],
  ['sortie-maries-voile-petales-jardins-coppelia-honfleur-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'The couple leaving under a shower of petals, veil in the wind, Honfleur'],
  ['danse-tendre-chateau-pont-chevron-ouzouer-sur-trezee-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'A tender dance at the château du Pont-Chevron in the Loire Valley'],
  ['violonistes-peniche-tour-eiffel-paris-nathanael-charpentier.jpg', 'Violinists playing on the barge facing the Eiffel Tower, Paris'],
].map(([f, a]) => ({ img: img(f), alt: a }));

const faq = [
  {
    q: 'How much does a high-end wedding photographer cost in France?',
    r: 'In France, a high-end wedding reportage runs between €2,500 and €5,000 for a full day. Nathanaël Charpentier photographs weddings from €2,700, one wedding per weekend. The fullest collection, L’Héritage, is €4,800: fourteen hours, from the preparations to the heart of the evening. La Signature, ten hours at €3,300, is the most requested. L’Expérience, six hours at €2,700, covers the core of the day.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Why is a professional wedding photographer so expensive?',
    r: 'A wedding cannot be done again, and that shapes the price far more than any list of costs. A photographer past the stage where attention is swallowed by settings can give it all to what matters: anticipating the moments that step out of the ordinary. That availability rests on bodies costing €3,000 to €6,000, at least two on the day, on training taken up again every year, and on one simple exclusivity: a single wedding per weekend. It continues long after the day itself, in post-production handled image by image, with no automatic filter.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What are the different wedding photography styles?',
    r: 'There are two axes worth keeping apart. In narrative: documentary, which keeps moments as they happen; editorial, borrowed from magazines; fashion, glamorous and directed; lifestyle, quieter and almost cinematic; fearless, which hunts the boldest angles. In treatment: light and airy with its pastel tones, dark and moody with its heavy contrast, and color-faithful, which respects the real colour of the scene — the most demanding of the three, since everything is decided at the moment of capture. With Nathanaël Charpentier the choice is made with the couple, according to what they love and what the day’s light allows.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you photograph weddings at Loire Valley châteaux?',
    r: 'Yes. Based in Gien, between the Sologne and the Loire Valley, an hour and a half from Paris, Nathanaël Charpentier photographs a limited number of château weddings each year, documentary-first. Collections from €2,700.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Where have you photographed weddings?',
    r: 'In the Loire Valley and the Sologne, in Paris and Normandy, and abroad: Corsica, Andalusia, Brussels, Marrakech, Mauritius and the Seychelles. Seven countries so far, and wherever he is invited.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you speak English?',
    r: 'Yes, enough to make your guests smile and your grandmother comfortable. Planning calls happen in English or French, as you prefer, and contracts are available in English.',
  },
];
---

<Base
  titre="Documentary wedding photographer in France — Loire Valley châteaux · Nathanaël Charpentier"
  description="Documentary wedding photography in France: your day exactly as it happened. Loire Valley châteaux, Paris, Normandy, Corsica. One wedding per weekend, from €2,700."
  lang="en"
  alterne="/mariage/"
  partage="mariage"
  partageAlt="Documentary wedding photography by Nathanaël Charpentier"
>
  <HeroDiaporama photos={photosHero} duree={4}>
    <h1 class="sur-image">Weddings</h1>
  </HeroDiaporama>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="contenu recit mesure">
      <p class="apparait">
        I was a musician before I was a photographer, and I tend to compare a wedding day to a jazz
        set: written passages (the ceremony, the speeches) and everything that invents itself in
        between. The first look. A father’s trembling hand. What your mother will only say once.
        These moments have no second take.
      </p>
      <p class="apparait">
        I am not a double bass player, but that is the role I like best on those days: the one who
        connects melody and rhythm, invisible and yet essential. That is the place I look for in
        your day. In the quiet moments I am forgotten; when the party rises, I am inside it.
      </p>
      <p class="apparait">
        I do not stage your day, and I do not interrupt it for one more picture. I photograph
        continuously, with no real break: the small moments that seem unremarkable on the day are
        often the ones that matter most ten years later.
      </p>
      <p class="apparait">
        Portrait work makes me better on the day itself. Guiding in a few words (a hand, a
        shoulder, where to rest your gaze) is learned in the studio, and it travels to every
        wedding. Most couples are not at ease in front of a lens; a few cues at the right moment,
        and the handful of posed pictures are done quickly, before the day is handed back to you.
      </p>
      <p class="apparait">
        Your photographs may look like a magazine’s: I care about light, framing and the texture
        of an image. But above all they will look like you: your gestures, your people, your day as
        it actually happened.
      </p>
      <p class="apparait">
        I take on a limited number of weddings each year, one per weekend. I like to disappear
        entirely into a day and give it everything, usually from the morning preparations to the
        last dance. That is what makes this way of working possible.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section sombre">
    <div class="contenu">
      <Galerie photos={photos} />
    </div>
  </section>

  <Faq items={faq} titre="Before you write" />
  <Invitation lang="en" phrase="Your day is being planned somewhere. Write me the date, the place, what you picture." />
</Base>

<style>
  .sur-image { color: var(--ivoire); }
  .recit { display: grid; gap: 1.9rem; }
</style>
